### `openclaw_direct__exec`
For continuous monitoring with future alerts, check automations for supported saved watchers. Ordinary background output cannot wake you to report new events. Run shell now; background continuation supported. Completed calls return command output directly. Use process only when exec reports running with a sessionId; output text alone is not a process handle. Long run: automatic completion wake, when enabled, occurs only after exit; otherwise process confirms completion. Output while still running does not automatically start another turn. Background commands can outlive the turn; use process kill when no longer needed. Completion and the configured timeout still apply; this is not a saved, restartable automation. Omit host/node to use the session's configured host. No sleep loops for reminders/follow-ups; use automations. TTY CLI/UI/coding agent: pty=true.
IMPORTANT (Windows): Run executables directly; do NOT wrap commands in `cmd /c`, `powershell -Command`, `& ` prefix, or WSL. Use backslash paths (C:\path), not forward slashes. Use short executable names (e.g. `node`, `python3`) instead of full paths.

