### `openclaw_direct__github_publish`
readiness: strictly observe the selected publishing session and optional existing requestId without credentials, refresh, source adoption, publication or recovery. Reports separate read policy, custody, bounded target support and shared receipt facts; write authority, authentication, exact remote destination, CI and mergeability remain unknown. A cwd is not a publication binding. Select an existing bound session, or separately authorize supported binding/adoption; observation never performs it. Pending or unconfirmed effects retain their original requestId: observe that request, never resubmit it. Accepts only action, publishingSessionKey and requestId. inspect_pr: supply pullRequestUrl to read an existing PR authored by your currently verified linked GitHub account. Accepts copied PR tab, query and comment links. Returns the canonical PR URL, author, state, base/head repositories, branches and observed commits. It does not prepare a workspace, bind the PR, publish changes or grant later authority. This is not a credential preflight for the managed publisher: bot-authored PRs need not belong to your linked account. Private repositories require verified current account access. Publish or edit the current session's PR through Gateway-held credentials, for local or cloud repository workspaces.
- publish (default when action is omitted): publish accepted workspace changes as an open PR by default; draft: true creates a draft. title/body and draft are used only when creating a PR. Updating an existing PR preserves its state. requested/publishing means accepted, not finished: retain requestId, finish the turn and await its result here; do not submit another publication to recover it. The receipt does not resume the agent. If authorized review, CI or landing remains, continue that work before ending the turn, or use automations to schedule a continuation when it offers add and the current caller is authorized (at + agentTurn + sessionTarget "session:<this session key from Runtime>"). While that scheduled continuation waits, use automations next_check to rearm its existing job, not add another job. If a scheduled continuation is unavailable, explain the remaining work; a receipt does not complete it.
- edit: read current metadata with {action: "edit"}, omitting expectedHeadCommit, title/body and expectedTitle/expectedBody. To change either field, send the read's top-level headCommit as expectedHeadCommit (not publication.headCommit), requestId when a publication receipt is returned, and its new value with the observed expectedTitle/expectedBody. Keep attribution, marker and footer unchanged in the full body. Omitted fields stay unchanged. Edit never synchronizes, stages, commits or pushes files or changes PR state. After an uncertain response, read again with only {action: "edit"} before retrying.
- ready: mark the current session's own draft ready for review, using the expectedHeadCommit and any publication requestId observed with edit. After an uncertain response, read with edit before retrying. This does not merge the PR.
- request_review: after an explicit re-review request, read the current PR with edit, then send expectedHeadCommit and any publication requestId to post only "@clawsweeper re-review". No comment text, focus or child target is accepted. Posting is not review acceptance or completion. If the response is uncertain, read existing PR comments before any new request; never retry blindly.
Edit, request_review and own-draft readiness accept no other repository, PR, ref or publishing session. For an explicit landing request from a person with full operator write access, use inspect, then ready and merge after review and required checks. For an explicit closure request, use close to close the PR without merging or deleting saved work. ready, merge and close require the inspected expectedHeadCommit and any publication requestId; merge also requires mergeMethod. For delegated work, explicitly select its publishingSessionKey from this conversation's children; never guess a PR. Actions return the observed GitHub state and never enable auto-merge. Inspect after an uncertain response before retrying. Inspect, merge, close and child selection require full operator write access. These actions also support a bound original PR: use its observed expectedHeadCommit without requestId when no publication receipt is returned. Actions do not change session sandboxing.

