```

### `openclaw_direct__openclaw`
Delegate system setup or repair to a separate model turn. Prefer your available tools for routine status and session/workspace checks. Gateway restart, config, channels, plugins, agents, models/providers, API keys. Supports multiple named custom/local model endpoints; provider IDs can be user-defined, while api selects the protocol. Setup flows use masked entry, which keeps keys out of model context; if the user already gave a key or token in chat, pass it along and OpenClaw stores it without echoing it. Changes wait for the user to approve in this chat (approval buttons or `/approve`) unless current Full Access or a standing delegation grant permits application without asking for approval. Returns the final outcome.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { openclaw_direct__openclaw(args: {
  // What system must do.
  message: string;
  // Continue prior OpenClaw talk.
  sessionId?: string;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `openclaw_direct__process`
Control existing exec: list, poll, log, write, send-keys, submit, paste, kill. poll/log: status, output, quiet success, completion without auto-wake, input hints. Others: input/intervention. kill requests termination or returns the retained terminal result for an already-finished session. After a termination request, poll until a terminal result confirms exit and cleanup before saying stopped. A running poll is still pending. remove hides the record and cannot confirm cleanup. Later process results supersede turn-start snapshots. Control sessions by sessionId; a displayed host PID is not a portable sandbox PID. No polling as timer/reminder; scheduled follow-up uses automations. On a requested monitoring stop, also stop any ordinary exec sessions you created for that request; stopping a saved automation does not stop them. Preserve unrelated work.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { openclaw_direct__process(args: {
  // Process action (list|poll|log|write|send-keys|submit|paste|kill|clear|remove)
  action: "list" | "poll" | "log" | "write" | "send-keys" | "submit" | "paste" | "kill" | "clear" | "remove";
  // Wrap paste in bracketed mode
  bracketed?: boolean;
  // Data to write for write
  data?: string;
  // Close stdin after write
  eof?: boolean;
  // Hex bytes to send for send-keys
  hex?: Array<string>;
  // Key tokens to send for send-keys
  keys?: Array<string>;
  // Log length
  limit?: number;
  // Literal string for send-keys
  literal?: string;
  // Log offset
  offset?: number;
  // Required for every action except list.
  sessionId?: string;
  // Text to paste for paste
  text?: string;
  // For poll: wait up to this many milliseconds before returning; max 30000 ms, higher values are clamped to 30000
  timeout?: number;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `openclaw_direct__sessions_yield`
End this turn to await pending child completions, not submit a final result. Return completed work normally. Does not message other sessions. Omit waitFor when yielding for your own children; their completions resume this session. Set waitFor:"message" only when a subagent has no pending children and waits for its requester to send it a continuation. For background tools, follow their continuation instructions. Automation turns end here; the scheduler delivers child output under the job delivery policy. Collector runs require explicit collection instead.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { openclaw_direct__sessions_yield(args: {
  // Optional brief waiting status shown to the user as your message; put answers in normal assistant text. With waitFor, also the task pause notice. Not an inter-session message.
  acknowledgment?: string;
  // Private context for the resumed turn; not sent to the user.
  message?: string;
  // Only for a subagent with no pending children of its own that waits for its requester to send it a continuation. Omit when yielding for your own children: their completions resume this session. Does not send or schedule that message or submit a final result.
  waitFor?: "message";
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `openclaw_direct__view_image`
Load image(s) into private model context for inspection: path accepts one local image path or permitted URL; paths accepts up to maxImages entries (20 by default). Does not display, attach, or send files to the user. Prompt images are already visible.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { openclaw_direct__view_image(args: {
  maxBytesMb?: number;
  maxImages?: number;
  // One local image path or permitted URL.
  path?: string;
  // Local image paths or permitted URLs; maxImages default 20.
  paths?: Array<string>;
  prompt?: string;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```
